Subject: [PATCH 08/10] .23 Execution Specification Builder: support full coin
 universe

Unlike .13-.19, this file already evaluated every symbol fully
independently -- one symbol's BLOCKED status never affected another's, or
the overall_status, beyond the ready_count tally -- so no new required-
vs-optional gating logic was needed, only widening the fixed BTC/ETH loop
to the full discovered coin universe:

- build_specs()'s main loop now iterates every symbol either the
  v0.5.3.13 signal or v0.5.3.19 safety payload reported (union with the
  new REQUIRED_SYMBOLS alias for BTC/ETH), instead of a fixed 2-symbol
  tuple.
- The shared-upstream-validation-failure branch (malformed/unverified
  signal or safety payload) now reports REQUIRED_SYMBOLS plus whatever
  symbols either payload's own decisions dict named, instead of silently
  dropping any symbol beyond BTC/ETH from that report.
- print_report() iterates actual decisions instead of a fixed BTC/ETH
  tuple, labeling each symbol REQUIRED/OPTIONAL.

Direction policy (empty-by-default allowlists, BEAR never implicitly
mapped to SELL), quantity policy (never fabricated, always from
--sizing-config), and the hard execution_authorized-must-already-be-True
boundary are all untouched by this change.

Adds 2 contract tests to the existing suite covering a symbol beyond the
required pair getting its own independent spec attempt (ready while
BTC/ETH stay blocked on an unvalidated direction) and an optional
symbol's own missing quantity blocking only that symbol. All 8 tests in
this file pass, including the existing BEAR-never-SELL and adapter-
interop tests, unchanged. Full suite (81 tests) green.

